# Integer16 literal above the maximum

Verifies an int16 literal one past the 16-bit maximum is rejected with a
compile-time diagnostic through the complete CLI pipeline.

>>> source
const too_large: int16 = 32768
print(too_large)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `32768` for type `int16`: number too large to fit in target type at Span { start: 25, end: 30 }

<<< exit
1
